Index the repository or manage global index registry

Usage: codesearch index [OPTIONS] [PATH] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  add      Add a repository to the index (creates local or global index)
  remove   Remove the index (local or global, auto-detected) [aliases: rm]
  list     Show index status (local, global, or on a remote peer) [aliases: ls]
  symbol   Rebuild symbol index (C# via scip-csharp) for a repository
  reindex  Reindex a repository (incremental, or full rebuild with --force)
  prune    Remove stale entries from repos.json (relocates moved repos first)
  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Arguments:
  [PATH]  Path to index (defaults to current directory) — used when no subcommand given

Options:
      --dry-run              Show what would be indexed without actually indexing
  -f, --force                Force full re-index
      --symbols              Also rebuild symbol index (C# via scip-csharp) after text reindex
      --add                  Add a repository to the index (creates local or global index)
  -g, --global               Create global index instead of local (only with --add)
      --remove               Remove the index (local or global, auto-detected) [aliases: --rm]
      --keep-config          Delete the DB only, preserve the config entry (only with --remove)
  -l, --loglevel <LOGLEVEL>  Set log level (error, warn, info, debug, trace) [default: info]
      --list                 Show index status (local or global)
  -q, --quiet                Suppress informational output (only show results/errors)
      --store <STORE>        Override default store name
      --model <MODEL>        Embedding model to use (e.g., bge-small, minilm-l6-q, jina-code) Available: minilm-l6, minilm-l6-q, minilm-l12, minilm-l12-q, paraphrase-minilm, bge-small, bge-small-q, bge-base, nomic-v1, nomic-v1.5, nomic-v1.5-q, jina-code, e5-multilingual, mxbai-large, modernbert-large
  -h, --help                 Print help
